EXPERIMENT 2 — GLIDER B
Prototype: Adjustable wing glider
Name: Glider B — Wide-Wing Design
Date started: 25th September 2026
Objective
To improve the design of Glider A and test whether a more stable design with greater wing area would improve flight performance.

Materials
A4 paper
Tape 

Design
I created a new glider with a wider wing area and a more stable structure.

Hypothesis
If I increase the wing area and improve the stability of the glider, then it should remain in the air longer and travel farther than Glider A.

Testing method
I performed 10 flight tests and measured:
Distance travelled in centimetres
Flight time in seconds

Results
Distance (cm)
Time (s)

